In the fifth beta of <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>, Apple is continuing to make design tweaks. There are updated Liquid Glass icons for Safari, the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> app, Settings, Remote, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/app-store/">App Store</a>, and Preview.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/ios-27-b5-icons.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059151" /><br/>
The Safari icon is a brighter blue with more detailed compass lines and arrows, while the &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; icon looks more like the actual &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; bubble that's displayed when &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; is activated. The &zwnj;App Store&zwnj; app icon is more translucent so you can better see each line making up the A, Settings uses more translucency, and Preview has an entirely different look with a loupe over a colorful background. The Remote icon also has more detail and it's been updated with a gray background instead of black.<br/>
<br/>
Some app icons were updated with the initial &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj; beta release, including Maps, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/photos/">Photos</a>, and Weather, but others kept their <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-26/">iOS 26</a> look.<br/>
<br/>
It's possible Apple will overhaul even more icons in upcoming betas, because the company said it was planning to give icons an updated layered look to better fit the Liquid Glass aesthetic.<br/>
